WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.760
Fermi's 14-year sky map has now catalogued 450 sources in the hard-to-reach Mi-V gamma-ray band. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 261. James Web imaged a stellar merger in Andromeda. A moon rocket engine was test-fired, and a caught starship is headed for a museum. The Fermi-large area telescope collaboration, according to Fizz.org, has produced the clearest view yet of low-energy gamma rays between 20 and 200 mega-electron volts.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.220
That slice of the spectrum had stayed a persistent blind spot because earlier instruments were

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.380
not sensitive enough to measure it reliably.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.560
The catalog is the first systematic bridge across what astronomers call the MeeVee Gap,

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.220
and the work appears in the Astrophysical Journal Supplement Series.

00:00:46.714 --> 00:00:52.394
Astronomers, Science Daily Reports, watched a small star spiral into a giant star 18,000

00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:55.354
times brighter than the Sun inside the Andromeda Galaxy.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:01:00.814
The collision produced a violent eruption, and the James Webb Space Telescope imaged that

00:01:00.814 --> 00:01:02.974
aftermath just 47 days later.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:08.214
The data give fresh detail on the physical processes that run when two stars merge into

00:01:08.214 --> 00:01:08.494
one.

00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:13.994
A powerful engine intended for the moon rocket of the National Aeronautics and Space Administration,

00:01:14.214 --> 00:01:17.754
or NASA, completed a 200-second hot fire test.

00:01:18.214 --> 00:01:22.874
The firing demonstrated sustained performance under conditions that simulate an actual lunar

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:23.554
mission burn.

00:01:23.554 --> 00:01:29.114
engineers will now analyze the data to confirm the engine meets requirements for crude flights.

00:01:29.614 --> 00:01:35.714
SpaceX founder Elon Musk, Space.com reports, said the first Starship upper stage grabbed by the

00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:40.934
launch tower's mechanical arms will not fly again. The vehicle will instead be preserved for

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:46.314
public display. That decision closes the flight chapter for that craft after the catch succeeded.

00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:53.147
Esar Aerospace Maritime Launch Services reports, has taken operational control of a dedicated

00:01:53.147 --> 00:01:58.987
launch complex at Space Port Nova Scotia and started building its own pad and assembly facilities.

00:01:59.507 --> 00:02:04.727
The site will support spectrum launches beginning in 2028 and gives Canada a second orbital

00:02:04.727 --> 00:02:10.087
launch location on its Atlantic coast. The Canadian government has backed the project as part of

00:02:10.087 --> 00:02:15.952
its sovereign space capability goals. Cypress opened the completed facilities of the Cypress Space

00:02:15.952 --> 00:02:21.652
Research and Innovation Center this week, Cypress Mail reports, including a mission control room

00:02:21.652 --> 00:02:26.832
and a space-weather operation center that uses artificial intelligence to forecast solar activity.

00:02:27.412 --> 00:02:31.372
Three locally-built Kyrenea 3 satellites were unveiled at the same time.

00:02:31.972 --> 00:02:36.972
Hungary's backup astronaut, Gula Cherigne attended the events and discuss plans for a space

00:02:36.972 --> 00:02:41.092
for schools program that would let students receive signals from the satellites.

00:02:41.672 --> 00:02:44.912
The center was co-funded by Cyprus and the European Union.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:51.111
Vandenberg Space Force Base is set for liftoff of the NRL 136 mission.

00:02:51.111 --> 00:02:56.111
1. Space flight now reports, a flight that will add satellites to the National Reconnaissance

00:02:56.111 --> 00:02:59.911
Office's proliferated architecture constellation in low-earth orbit.

00:03:00.351 --> 00:03:04.251
The flight marks the fourth such launch this year and the 15th overall.

00:03:04.891 --> 00:03:10.411
Lift off from Space Launch Complex 4E is scheduled for 4.23am Pacific Standard Time.

00:03:10.991 --> 00:03:17.691
Falcon 9 booster B1097 will fly its 14th mission and target a landing at landing zone 4,

00:03:17.691 --> 00:03:23.351
which would be the 38th landing at that site and the 680th Falcon booster landing overall.

00:03:24.274 --> 00:03:29.794
Amanda Wynn, the first Vietnamese woman in space, Sirisha Bandla, the third Indian woman

00:03:29.794 --> 00:03:35.394
in space, and Sian Leo Proctor, the first black female spacecraft pilot, according to

00:03:35.394 --> 00:03:38.954
the Cambridge Somerville Independent, spoke at the Museum of Science.

00:03:39.454 --> 00:03:44.234
They described the overview effect and credited commercial spaceflight with increasing diversity

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:45.794
in gender, age, and race.

00:03:45.794 --> 00:03:51.534
The panel was moderated by astronomer Athena Brensberger and included discussion of privately

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:55.354
funded missions from Blue Origin, Virgin Galactic and SpaceX.

00:03:56.479 --> 00:04:01.999
In brief, Senator Ted Cruz, the Hill reports, says he is already working with Representative

00:04:01.999 --> 00:04:05.299
Joaquin Castro to bring a space academy program to Texas.

00:04:05.999 --> 00:04:11.559
Kennedy Space Center visitor complex, Jalopnik reports, is building an indoor roller coaster

00:04:11.559 --> 00:04:17.119
called Arrow Test Lab that will open in 2028 and simulate NASA flight test scenarios.

00:04:17.659 --> 00:04:22.999
A team at the Trahtier Institute for Research on Exoplanets, in shorts reports, found an

00:04:22.999 --> 00:04:27.239
unusual triple-star system just 28 light years away while searching for planets.

00:04:27.779 --> 00:04:32.399
The system, named Welopoi, holds two white dwarfs and one red dwarf.

00:04:32.899 --> 00:04:37.039
Researchers say that arrangement should not exist, since the white dwarfs would have

00:04:37.039 --> 00:04:39.359
disturbed the red dwarf as they evolved earlier.

00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:44.099
precise radial velocity data showed speed changes far larger than planets

00:04:44.099 --> 00:04:48.279
alone would produce. Professor Patrick Dufour said the layout challenges

00:04:48.279 --> 00:04:52.979
current models of how stars interact in close multiples. The system gives a

00:04:52.979 --> 00:04:58.532
nearby laboratory for testing how binary and triple stars form. Gamma rays are

00:04:58.532 --> 00:05:02.772
the highest energy light in the electromagnetic spectrum, but a wide slice of

00:05:02.772 --> 00:05:07.112
that range has been stubbornly hard to chart. Photons in that band are too

00:05:07.112 --> 00:05:12.152
energetic for conventional X-ray telescopes and too soft for the large area detectors

00:05:12.152 --> 00:05:17.392
built for higher energy gamma rays. Detectors could not gather enough clean photons for

00:05:17.392 --> 00:05:22.952
reliable sky maps, leaving a hole right where many astrophysical processes should shine brightest.

00:05:23.692 --> 00:05:28.632
A long integration let the team pull faint celestial signals out of instrumental and cosmic

00:05:28.632 --> 00:05:34.352
ray background that had swamped earlier data. Because the telescope orbits above the atmosphere,

00:05:34.352 --> 00:05:38.392
it avoids the absorption that blocks these photons from reaching the ground.

00:05:38.992 --> 00:05:43.712
The catalog shows where the sources sit, not which physics dominates at these energies

00:05:43.712 --> 00:05:45.792
or how those sources change with time.

00:05:46.472 --> 00:05:51.732
Future instruments that can measure polarization or rapid variability in the same band would

00:05:51.732 --> 00:05:56.592
help pin down whether the emission comes from pulsar magnetospheres, active galactic

00:05:56.592 --> 00:05:59.032
nuclei, or something entirely unexpected.

00:05:59.032 --> 00:06:03.732
Until those measurements arrive, that sky stays only partly charted.

00:06:04.517 --> 00:06:09.397
Casting back over the last seven days, NASA said the first images from the Nancy Grace

00:06:09.397 --> 00:06:12.537
Roman Space Telescope will arrive on December 7th.

00:06:13.037 --> 00:06:17.577
University of Sydney researchers found that the Milky Way's central bar is sparking new

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:19.077
stars along its shock fronts.

00:06:19.777 --> 00:06:24.057
Seven spacecraft are set to track how energy from the sun moves through Earth's magnetic

00:06:24.057 --> 00:06:24.497
shield.

00:06:25.057 --> 00:06:27.037
That's fascinating frontiers for today.

